<title>SWEDEN: Sydkraft posts Q1 profit 3.40 bln Skr.</title>
<headline>Sydkraft posts Q1 profit 3.40 bln Skr.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish power group Sydkraft</p>
<p>on Friday posted these earnings for the first three months of</p>
<p>the year, ending on March 31.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Profit after fin items</p>
<p> including capital gain		  3,404 vs   976</p>
<p> Capital gain				2,303 vs   nil</p>
<p> Net sales				   4,359 vs 4,149</p>
<p>Earnings per share excluding</p>
<p> capital gain (crowns)		    3.95 vs 3.70</p>
<p> Operating costs			   2,711 vs 2,703</p>
<p> Depreciation				  373 vs   326</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	 1,427 vs 1,198</p>
<p>Financial income including</p>
<p> capital gain				2,415 vs   101</p>
<p> Financial costs			     438 vs   323</p>
<p> Minorities					7 vs     6</p>
<p> Tax					     983 vs   261</p>
<p> Net profit				  2,414 vs   709</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts in a Reuter poll expected Sydkraft to post a profit after financial items of 3.29 billion crowns, including a capital gain of 2.2 billion crowns, deriving from the sale of shares in German utility VEBA.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
